# Citation metadata for this repository.
#
# GitHub reads this file and shows a "Cite this repository" button in the sidebar.
# Zenodo reads .zenodo.json instead, so the two must be kept in step: if you change an
# author, a title or the version here, change it there too.
#
# After the first release is archived, fill in the two fields marked TODO with the
# concept DOI Zenodo mints (the one that always resolves to the latest version, not the
# version-specific DOI), and add the same DOI badge to README.md.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Weeklies: variety-driven, budget- and nutrition-aware meal planning"
abstract: >-
  A Flask web application that plans a week of meals. A plan must satisfy every hard
  rule -- allergies, dietary requirements, restaurant opening hours, stock, and an
  exact-cents weekly budget cap -- and among the plans that do, the planner picks the
  one with the most variety across cuisine, protein, carb base and cooking method. Days
  can additionally be aimed at calorie, protein, carb, fat and sodium ranges, estimated
  from USDA FoodData Central's Survey (FNDDS) 2024-10-31 release.
type: software
license: MIT
version: 3.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-25"
repository-code: "https://github.com/fixmeseb/Weeklies"
url: "https://fixmeseb.github.io/Weeklies/"
# doi: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX   # TODO: concept DOI, after the first release is archived
keywords:
  - meal planning
  - combinatorial optimization
  - local search
  - constraint satisfaction
  - nutrition
  - Flask
  - software engineering education

authors:
